# Line endings are pinned, not left to each machine's git config.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows default, and what this
# project is actually developed on) checks every text file out with CRLF while
# the repository itself stores LF. Prettier is configured for `endOfLine: "lf"`,
# so it rejects the working copy it was just handed — `npm run format:check`
# goes red on Windows for files that are perfectly formatted, and green on the
# Linux CI runner for the same commit. That split is worse than either result:
# it trains you to ignore the check locally.
#
# `eol=lf` makes the checkout match what is stored, on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never touch these, whatever the extension heuristics guess.
*.png binary
*.bmp binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.gguf binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.node binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.zip binary
